# Database migrations

Start PostgreSQL from the repository root with `docker compose up -d db`.
Compose publishes PostgreSQL on host port `5433`; set `DATABASE_URL` in
`backend\.env` to match the local template in `backend\.env.example`.

Apply migrations from the backend directory:

```powershell
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m alembic upgrade head
```

The second migration adds the simplified task-board table. Older schema tables
are left in place to avoid deleting any data.